            0.77,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Metallic oxides of zinc, magnesium and copper were heated with the following metals.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.178,
            0.678,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.174,
                0.178,
                0.678,
                0.277
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>Metal</td><td>Zinc</td><td>Magnesium</td><td>Copper</td></tr><tr><td>Zinc oxideMagnesium oxideCopper oxide</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.287,
            0.739,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In which cases will you find displacement reactions taking place?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.971,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.309,
            0.491,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Which metals do not corrode easily?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.331,
            0.324,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. What are alloys?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.391,
            0.54,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What you have learnt"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.436,
            0.654,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Elements can be classified as metals and non-metals.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.456,
            0.891,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals are lustrous, malleable, ductile and are good conductors of heat and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "electricity. They are solids at room temperature, except mercury which is a liquid.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.494,
            0.743,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals can form positive ions by losing electrons to non-metals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.514,
            0.892,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals combine with oxygen to form basic oxides. Aluminium oxide and zinc oxide "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "show the properties of both basic as well as acidic oxides. These oxides are known as amphoteric oxides.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.568,
            0.794,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Different metals have different reactivities with water and dilute acids.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.589,
            0.891,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A list of common metals arranged in order of their decreasing reactivity is known "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "as an activity series.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.626,
            0.891,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals above hydrogen in the Activity series can displace hydrogen from dilute acids.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.663,
            0.833,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A more reactive metal displaces a less reactive metal from its salt solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.684,
            0.836,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals occur in nature as free elements or in the form of their compounds.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.704,
            0.892,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The extraction of metals from their ores and then refining them for use is known "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "as metallurgy.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.742,
            0.892,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An alloy is a homogeneous mixture of two or more metals, or a metal and a non-metal.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.779,
            0.891,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The surface of some metals, such as iron, is corroded when they are exposed to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "moist air for a long period of time. This phenomenon is known as corrosion.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.816,
            0.891,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Non-metals have properties opposite to that of metals. They are neither malleable "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "nor ductile. They are bad conductors of heat and electricity, except for graphite, which conducts electricity.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.916,
            0.269,
            0.93
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metals and Non-metals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 22,
